{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789373179,"nonce":"Z9uWWvtYfPa3mbJjbKmOdGIo0vs=","title":"The library's HIR is decoded whole on the first import: 12 ms of a 43 ms hello world","message":"`zypy run hello.py`, cold, `ZYNTAX_TRACE_LOWER_PHASES=1`:\n\n    parse      10 to 13 ms    of which ruff and inference are under 0.5 ms;\n                              the rest is Snapshot::module(\"builtins\"):\n                              typed program 1.2 to 2.1 ms (257 KB, CBOR),\n                              HIR 11 to 12 ms (978 KB, postcard)\n    runtime     0.3 ms\n    register    0.07 ms\n    compile    28 to 33 ms    (ca69295)\n    run         0.5 ms\n\nThe parser is not the cost. The HIR of all 422 library functions is\ndecoded on the first import, though the typed program is all the parser\nneeds and a program adopts about 30 of the functions (4c5c7b1). The\ndecode is serde over `IndexMap\u003cHirId, HirValue\u003e` and\n`IndexMap\u003cHirId, HirBlock\u003e` per function: allocation volume, no single\nhot spot.\n\nFix: decode function bodies on demand. The snapshot carries the module\nskeleton (globals, types, signatures) as one blob and each function's\nbody as its own extent; `Snapshot::module` decodes the skeleton, and the\nlinker's `adopt_prelowered_reached` asks for a body when a call reaches\nit. `HirId` relocation has to use one base for the whole module, fixed\nwhen the skeleton is decoded, with the counter advanced past the\nmodule's highest id up front (recorded by the build like max_type_id).\nAlso a bytecode format version.\n\nDecoding on a background thread started at process entry hides only\nthe 2 to 3 ms the parse takes; measured as not worth the machinery on\nits own.","files":null}]}